<!--ID=B7267351-473F-409D-9765-754A8EBCDE05;Version=1|{"VoiceNameToIdMapItems":[{"Id":"f1b99834-fbfc-4d32-846d-c4dbd3050c19","Name":"Microsoft Server Speech Text to Speech Voice (en-GB, OllieMultilingualNeural)","ShortName":"en-GB-OllieMultilingualNeural","Locale":"en-GB","VoiceType":"StandardVoice"}]}-->
<!--ID=FCB40C2B-1F9F-4C26-B1A1-CF8E67BE07D1;Version=1|{"Files":{}}-->
<!--ID=5B95B1CC-2C7B-494F-B746-CF22A0E779B7;Version=1|{"Locales":{"en-US":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]},"en-GB":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]}}}-->
<speak xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2001/10/synthesis"
       xmlns:mstts="http://www.w3.org/2001/mstts"
       xmlns:emo="http://www.w3.org/2009/10/emotionml"
       version="1.0"
       xml:lang="en-GB">
  <voice name="en-GB-OllieMultilingualNeural">
    <prosody rate="-10.00%" pitch="-2.00%">
      Take a slow breath in.<break time="500ms"/>
      And let it out gently.<break time="1000ms"/>
      Again, breathe in.<break time="500ms"/>
      And breathe out.<break time="1800ms"/>

      Let your forehead soften.<break time="500ms"/>
      Let your shoulders drop.<break time="500ms"/>
      Let the weight of the day loosen its grip.<break time="1000ms"/>
      There is nowhere you need to hurry now.<break time="1800ms"/>

      Tonight we will rest inside one of the gentlest songs in the book of Psalms.<break time="500ms"/>
      A shepherd song.<break time="1000ms"/>
      A song for tired minds, tired bodies, and hearts that want quiet.<break time="1800ms"/>

      The Psalms do not begin here with pressure.<break time="500ms"/>
      They begin with presence.<break time="500ms"/>
      The Lord is near.<break time="1000ms"/>
      The Lord is guiding.<break time="1000ms"/>
      The Lord is keeping watch.<break time="1800ms"/>

      In a shepherd song, rest comes by hearing what is true more than once.<break time="500ms"/>
      Nearness.<break time="1000ms"/>
      Provision.<break time="1000ms"/>
      Guidance.<break time="1000ms"/>
      Care.<break time="1800ms"/>

      You do not have to force an image.<break time="500ms"/>
      You do not have to hold every line in your mind.<break time="500ms"/>
      Just let the rhythm carry you.<break time="1000ms"/>
      Let the Shepherd walk at an unhurried pace beside you.<break time="1800ms"/>

      If a thought rises, let it pass softly.<break time="500ms"/>
      If your body is still busy, let it settle slowly.<break time="500ms"/>
      The song will keep moving, one calm phrase at a time.<break time="1800ms"/>

      And as we enter it, remember only this.<break time="500ms"/>
      You are not alone in the night.<break time="1000ms"/>
      You are safe in the Shepherd's care.<break time="1800ms"/>
    </prosody>
  </voice>
</speak>
